[Music]  the twins du Cheval was to France what  the Volkswagen Beetle was to Germany  mobility for the masses it was designed  in the 1930s to help French farmers who  still relied on horses and carts as our  classic car expert christoph bauer  explains he says citron boss Pierre  Bouchet had concrete ideas about the car  it should have room for two farmers and  a sack of potatoes and do at least 60  kilometres an hour yet have such a  comfortable suspension that a basket of  eggs could survive journeys over bumpy  fields unscathed it should be easy to  operate but looks weren't important in  1939 sat.1 began making prototypes of  the tpv as it was then called for toot  petit fuller or very small car though  not terribly attractive they met belong  J's criteria even passing the test with  a basket of eggs third designer Flamini  Alberto nee was told to keep the car  functional he was instructed to create  an umbrella on four wheels christophe  says that after the end of the second  world war Bertoni was allowed to gussy  up the body a little in 1948 the do  cheveux finally made its debut but  response was lukewarm the press dubbed  the car a sardine can  or even worse an ugly duckling Oh Lala  in Germany the name stuck to this day  the car is lovingly called tienta or the  duck these are spitzy from a dog  into good allah school in france the car  quickly became a favorite and why not  after all it was designed to meet the  wishes of the public as expressed in one  of the first big market surveys  conducted in 1922 then tire manufacture  missional asked 10,000 people what their  ideal car would look like christophe  says it'd be hard to build a more basic  car than the do cheveux  to him the seats resembled camping  chairs the windows don't roll down you  swing them out and hook them on here hmm  and you can hardly call this a dashboard  it's just a couple of pieces of sheet  metal that have been cobbled together  interestingly the main instrument here  is the battery indicator the speedometer  is stuck here in the corner strangely  enough the speedometer cable  simultaneously powers the windshield  wipers so if a rains hard you should put  your foot on the gas so I wanted a stick  ask him  cathodic huh fabulous Christophe says  the do cheveux is built on a box frame  on which all of the body parts are  mounted so like the VW Beetle it doesn't  employ unibody construction and as you  can tell from the protruding wings and  hood-mounted headlights it's old  fashioned design dates from the  pre-world war ii era but it's huge soft  top also makes it into a convertible  what sounds like a luxury was at the  time nothing but a cost-cutting measure  a sheet metal was in short supply in the  post-war he rocked in click of our start  list its demand Ibaka sat when never  tried to pass off its ugly duckling as a  beautiful swan its ads said the cars  shape was unusual but that it's  performance was second to none the  vehicles legendary suspension with its  longitudinal coil springs make the do  cheveux feel like no other on the road  the Spartan trunk can hold many sacks of  potatoes while the rollback canvas roof  puts in plenty of fresh air inside the  simplest of seats and the unfinished  looking cockpit complete the minimalist  look ta-dah Malta and Krista says under  the hood you'll find the two cylinder  425 CC box er engine with an output of  just 12 horsepower you can't get much  lower than that although the first  douche of OHS at just 9 horsepower yet  the engine was progressive for its time  to reduce weight the cylinder heads and  cylinder block were made entirely from  aluminum and he says it's the only car  he knows that you could start with a  crank that was still in production in  1990 said twin even considered doing  without an ignition switch in starter  motor the reason that it was a car for  farmers who all had wives to turn the  crank so much for equal opportunity  even the douche avos with the most  powerful engines have a hard time  breaking the 100 kilometer an hour  barrier going from 0 to 100 takes 30 to  40 seconds yet there's no time to get  bored  Christophe says the douche avos off-road  capabilities and hair-raising cornering  are legendary if you push it the card  tips so far to the side that you think  it's going to tip over but it doesn't  it's boxer engine makes for an extremely  low center of gravity so it's almost  impossible for the do cheveux to flip  over back in 1967 sits when considered  stopping production but the do cheveux  survived and continued to roll off the  assembly lines until 1988 in France and  1990 in Portugal in its later years the  models horsepower increased to 28 3  times as much as the original douche  avos Vigo Christoph says it's hard to  make a car with less the new shahboz  technology was extremely basic and it  cost almost nothing to run that turned  this anti status symbol into a  much-loved status symbol for students  anti-nuclear activists and  environmentalists more than 5 million  were built over four decades he feels  the do shovel symbolizes savoir view the  French Way of life like no other car  which makes it a true milestone in  automotive history it's low maintenance  costs and robust technology have made  this suit one an enduring classic  despite its small engine and minimal  cubic capacity some drivers have clocked  up 300,000 kilometers in their do  shallows not bad for an umbrella on four  wheels

